    "notes": "the js-stellar-sdk#1766 issuers: 32 bytes of 0x3a sort first as strkey text (GA5D... before GAAA...), 32 zero bytes sort first as key bytes, which is what core uses. same code on both sides, so the issuer decides. expected order computed with core's rule (asset type, code bytes with zero padding, issuer key bytes; isPoolShareAssetValid in stellar-core v30.0.0 src/util/types.cpp and the xdrpp union and xarray comparisons it uses), checked against stellar-xdr's derived Ord. pool_id cases expect the id core derives (sha256 of LiquidityPoolParameters with fee 30) when a < b, and a refusal otherwise, because core answers CHANGE_TRUST_MALFORMED for parameters that are not strictly ordered.",
